{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47fef80094391c2437170ee9591bb62dcae59777d1aece1a0f6b83c1316b86d8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2daf23f525a6790c92c9c39d905f0e63b13e969bf3cb077c1489a346fb2685c0","slc_64601b44c42bad81df87e63266f81f62ad5b959343fa4c40895454f62934ff71","slc_9fdcdf35b4dce4dbb5d8037dcf8e92daf5b8ac6da86f7a6f10069ecc58df756a"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Persistent memory is stored locally in SQLite via Node's built-in node:sqlite at ~/.damocles/memory.v3.db, with no native modules or WASM, and memories carry kinds (fact, preference, episode, observation, note) and scopes (session, project, global).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_521af124767126478ffb358729d67396f947405e47d006902d46adf5307673d0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b4edf2aa66f2aade5ed003c21b2454acd773392a49dc15edc008a56835c675a4","slc_c52ebf0749c99b4d9db8568420835ffffbd28e2cd92cd287efaf21d50f7c8060"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Slash commands include built-ins like /clear, /compact, /rewind, /remember, /note, /memories, /context and /usage, plus custom commands loaded from .damocles/commands, .claude/commands and .codex/prompts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_54a8928c5972ed34934134324b4298e09dbfaec30ec8ccfb9c6b7a13cc8cc3f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_077ccf89d4d77882cca77ddc502b6f8510c152483fb4378ab0e366bd3658f19e","slc_ddead421c871e5928a85939363a00e61bad4231cffaded8e004384dfc20585d6"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"The agent has ten autonomous memory tools, including save_memory, save_observation, search_memories, get_memory_details, get_memory_history, get_related_memories, forget_memory, save_note/list_notes, and reset_observation_staleness.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6d8f5f2a1c2e1548468efaadf8a5075be93afe19f1149fcf7ffebabcda387a0c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4eae7c41a600e6262344a8dd9a98237e6a057e92e6d885d7593049752dde9e0a","slc_7b301893769ce48827705434ce5b0e368c207f7f7e7086003c9c3054b9579298","slc_d2d687e03e5c4c3f580d518fb0b01bf92ba3943338ac4eb7aa3a8cd449929e83","slc_fe17ec6f62f753644da156f0a36b0fc2b83eb475a86fd28eac064a9b82e2b032"],"source_ids":["src_12ea332d5fa55ffea280f61060eba534","src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Hook safety is bounded by workspace trust: the global ~/.damocles/hooks.json is always honored while the project-level file is honored only in a trusted workspace, and both files hot-reload on change with global running before project.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_942c896eb8862499e4aad38d8e9a7b8749fc3ca92fa94d1ebe27ba0b38d37f76","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b16f8e46842ebad1cc05029bfbc69a2b33c9cf366d70bd1224b6e5fc223ec59b"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Requirements include VS Code 1.95.0+, a Claude or ChatGPT/Codex subscription or respective API keys, plus StepFun and DeepSeek provider keys; supported platforms are Windows, macOS, and Linux.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a071ff44888d7b7771dc1187540e4751fb5a9d451b6a19c278f80dccf9960cda","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b25241db89d4a5e807450eaf74ab6438c7b623f694ecff4c4bd9ba2c5ed2777f"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Damocles runs on the pi agent engine and talks to Anthropic and OpenAI directly, keeping its own credentials under ~/.damocles/ isolated from the Claude Code CLI, whose settings and skills it reads but whose credentials it never touches.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a1bf26e521f7dd1353a5b3a9711685b790a7e9f20a9bc82ecb9a8f335d7d89f1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7a9c23725ab400536f67d076c672d1efad142f78869bdc9a822870c6ef19632a","slc_fd9394453387239dfb4d2b45b1dce837e9e1f43675eae62e6b998754cad51abf"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Project-scope commands, skills, and instruction files are gated on VS Code workspace trust so an untrusted repository cannot inject prompts or hooks; user-scope assets remain unaffected.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_af6a86650e68ad7010a659d641dd17d6cbb5f3439a8f5a7c587dedda7b2347f7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_afc347038600ff16d52e4e66addc10d89cef07ffccf6d3820154c15a3ec33caa"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"The architecture consists of a Node.js extension host running the pi engine, tools, and permissions; a Vue 3 + Tailwind webview chat interface; and a postMessage bridge between them.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_af80da6bb2397e1139b09ed13a77dc3be51ae77566bc03abac4ba6e7d8bbef9b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_18d19ee572d4b82d8dcf4197e63868bc9368ac446af19aa87ed1d85dbc06a90d"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Keyboard shortcuts include Ctrl+K for a prompt navigator, Shift+Tab to cycle permission modes, Escape to cancel a request, and double-Escape to open a rewind popup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b22f0df364552cc5d98281b7335d751806dcf3e364d46417aa805d8e8b40ceea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7756ef291b42a91495ee99b970db60141335de05602352daf3c1abb78ed6c3d0","slc_9c3975fd6ece093cd9273b2fc5bd17cf4bab64be627737a2b64f38befbe68a41"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Bash and PowerShell permission rules are evaluated independently, so a Bash rule never auto-allows an equivalent PowerShell command; pattern syntax covers shell prefixes plus Edit(*.ts) and Write(src/**) style file patterns.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b87671e4d7b2e0c90c18f069f8789d34c4580f786628aa82a44708289831045a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_811af96ae6924f53ef12f4b2704e6bbbce664d63a64ac7d444f2c48c23fd0a0c"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Asset precedence is builtin > .damocles > .claude/.codex, with project overriding user within a scope and damocles.assetSourcePrecedence (default claude) breaking ties between compat sources; matching is case-insensitive.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bc47b01d4d285a04ca62fe9a1223077d1ee2119bbdc25adda6f5dd2ce45ebc34","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_413a1a0971186f509993d66d67d8f25a0c72e3eebabf2240cd15fe2680f5bc3c","slc_44e2ff3ae891884a9dd8da687ec74b8c4886dbfb732786cd9f84d88649220d42","slc_e11c9f7f7053fa2c001f68db543f85abdfee498ca9355d11adf517d791afda3b"],"source_ids":["src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Persistent allow/deny/ask permission rules are evaluated before each tool call, read from an eight-tier priority chain of .damocles and .claude settings files where the first match wins; Damocles writes only to .damocles/.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c66a49b9f4185d8862fb7d4b737c35563621dfbcf120ee9f387837ccb801fdb4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"aizenvoltprime/damocles@b8787a5e9b69 snapshot 87e325b5b99a6e04","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4121646c377513af9d07afe60fcf625eee7cdae927c80badd378ed2cfe0c777d","slc_b8c1a84b720d32b279d48c6fb9932a5c58f7075f3a3b8c2dd747b0dae3c971fb","slc_e564ba7794d1fda8d43ff7d4fbfa12d00414b1ab888f067086195941c9edda47"],"source_ids":["src_12ea332d5fa55ffea280f61060eba534","src_6f3f4ffccf0b5c7e9050cce7ca22f6e7"],"text":"Hooks let users run their own commands at session events via hooks.json; the child process receives one JSON object on stdin and replies with one on stdout, and a tool_call hook can block, force-allow, or rewrite a tool call.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:30:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f90d6e44959d46e085cbff70119051a9"}
